# Line-ending policy across the nix-config tree.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows (with the default git
# `core.autocrlf=true`) silently rewrites every `.sh` / `.nix` / `.md`
# to CRLF on checkout, which breaks bash on every line:
#   /mnt/c/.../mattpc-wsl-bootstrap.sh: line 36: $'\r': command not found
#
# Pin everything to LF including PowerShell — pwsh 7+ handles LF on
# Windows fine, and the previous `eol=crlf` carve-out for *.ps1 was
# load-bearing only for Windows PowerShell 5.1 edge cases we no longer
# hit. It also fights jj, which doesn't run smudge/clean filters and
# would see every checkout-rewritten line as modified.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — git should never touch these for line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.tgz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
